NO LOGINS: System going down at %5.5s

␀␀␀/etc/nologin␀␀␀␀/fastboot␀␀␀@8␀␀␀␀ ␀␀␀␀␀␀„␀␀␀␀X␀␀„␀␀,␀␀X␀␀,␀␀,␀␀´␀␀␀x␀␀␀<␀␀␀<␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀???␀shutdown␀shutdown: '%c' - unknown flag
␀Usage: shutdown [ -krhfn ] shutdowntime [ message ]
␀shutdown: Incompatible switches 'fast' & 'nosync'
␀NOT super-user
␀ ␀Shutdown at %5.5s (in ␀%d hour%s ␀s␀␀%d minute%s) ␀s␀␀[pid %d]
␀␀/etc/utmp␀shutdown: /etc/utmp␀FINAL ␀sleeper␀w␀

␀	...%s␀
System shutdown time has arrived
␀%s by %s: %s␀reboot␀halt␀shutdown␀but you'll have to do it yourself
␀/etc/reboot␀reboot␀-l␀/etc/halt␀halt␀-l␀now␀That must be tomorrow
Can't you wait till then?
␀Bad time format
